      "modelAnswer": "Compare a₁/a₂, b₁/b₂ and c₁/c₂. If a₁/a₂ ≠ b₁/b₂ the lines cross once (e.g. x + y = 5, x − y = 1). If a₁/a₂ = b₁/b₂ ≠ c₁/c₂ they are parallel with no solution (x + y = 5, 2x + 2y = 7). If all three ratios are equal the lines coincide and there are infinitely many solutions (x + y = 5, 2x + 2y = 10).",
